    {"id": 11, "type": "manual", "slot": "(b)",
     "desc": "Part (b): a correct response says that without a restriction the rule v is not one-to-one -- the parabola with vertex at (3, -4) takes each output twice, once on each side of x = 3 (for instance both inputs give the same value), so no single rule can send an output back to one input. Keeping x >= 3 selects the increasing half, which is one-to-one, and that is why the inverse uses only the plus square root. Full credit needs the one-to-one idea and a reference to the vertex or to the two inputs sharing an output.",
